# Wiki / knowledge — local-first

Используй проверенный локальный снимок General Wiki как базу. Обычная индексация
не обращается к Notion. Любое чтение или изменение внешней Wiki выполняется
только по явной просьбе или отдельной команде с обязательным read-back.
Автоматизации на commit/PR пока нет.

## Base (always)

- Source of truth for agents: `docs/knowledge/` (local General Wiki snapshot).
- Selective reading: `AGENT_PROTOCOL.md` → `INDEX.md` → matching `areas/*.md`.
- After structural code changes: update local knowledge + `npm run knowledge:check`.
  Do **not** call Notion or push GitHub Wiki unless the user asked.

## External Wiki (Notion / GitHub Wiki)

Allowed **only** when the user explicitly asks or names a dedicated command
(`knowledge:wiki`, `knowledge:notion`, “обнови Notion”, “sync wiki”, etc.).

Then:

1. Perform the requested read and/or write.
2. **Read-back** — re-fetch or re-read the external page and confirm the result
   to the user (what changed / what was read).
3. Never treat external Wiki as the index for ordinary code work.

## No commit/PR automation

Do not add or rely on commit hooks / PR checks that sync external wikis.
CI may still run local `knowledge:check`. Wiki sync workflows stay manual
(`workflow_dispatch`) only.
